        "PERENNIAL FRUIT: mature and ancient stages auto-yield apples each autumn via fruit_harvest.",
        "Fruit harvest is NON-DESTRUCTIVE \u00e2\u20ac\u201d tree persists. Chop harvest gives wood + seeds only.",
        "Four seasonal models: spring (blossom), summer (leafy), autumn (gold/rust), winter (bare).",
        "Footprint follows the spreading-tree rule \u00e2\u20ac\u201d see 42_farming_brewing.md \u00c2\u00a7 Surface Trees.",
        "",
        "MODEL VARIANTS (mature and ancient only \u00e2\u20ac\u201d same rule as oak):",
        "  Ancient: summer x3, autumn x2, spring x1, winter x1.",
        "  Mature: approved single models in every season and fruiting state (doc 27); older alternates are no longer selected.",
        "  The autumn_fruiting model is a SEPARATE key; the world spawner currently selects it throughout autumn when fruit_harvest exists.",
        "  It is always single \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no variants for the fruiting overlay state."
      ],
